!!! The accept loop.
!!!
!!! Everything above this module works on text: a request arrives as text and
!!! a response leaves as text, which is what makes a handler testable with no
!!! server running. This is the one place that touches a socket, and it is
!!! deliberately the only one.
!!!
!!! One connection at a time. There are no threads to hand a connection to,
!!! no async in the language and no way to wait on several sockets at once, so
!!! this accepts, serves, closes, and goes round again. That is enough for a
!!! development server, a local tool, or anything behind a reverse proxy that
!!! absorbs the slow clients, and it is honest about what it is rather than
!!! appearing to scale and then not.
!!!
!!! The caller owns dispatch. `serve-once` reads a request, hands the text to
!!! whatever the application does with it, and writes the answer back, so the
!!! routing, the templates and the sessions above are reached by the
!!! application's own paragraph rather than by a callback this module holds —
!!! Matrix has no capturing closures, so a callback is not available to hold.

book nilweb.server.listener

read nil.std.core
read nil.std.net.socket
read nil.std.text
read nil.std.text.string_utils
read everything from nilweb.text.scan
read everything from nilweb.http.headers


!!! How long a connection may stay silent before it is dropped.
!!!
!!! Not optional. A single-threaded loop with no deadline is one open-and-say-
!!! nothing connection away from serving nobody, and that is as easy to do by
!!! accident with a port scanner as on purpose.
constant silence-limit-ms as number is 15000

!!! The most a request may be, header and body together.
!!!
!!! A ceiling here rather than at the parser, because the point is to stop
!!! reading rather than to reject afterwards. 1 MiB is generous for a form and
!!! far below anything that would trouble the process.
constant request-limit as number is 1048576

!!! One read per pass. Large enough that an ordinary request arrives whole.
constant chunk-size as number is 65536


public bound-server begin record
    field listener as number
    field listening as boolean
    field complaint as text
end record


!!! --- Bind a port, or say why not.
!!!
!!! The host is passed through to the intrinsic, which takes numeric, empty or
!!! localhost and will not resolve a name. "127.0.0.1" during development;
!!! empty for every interface, which is a decision to make deliberately.

public bind-server receives host as text, port as number returns bound-server begin paragraph
    value opened is nil.std.net::listen with host being host, port being port, backlog being 64
    consider opened
        when Result.Ok holding handle then
            give build bound-server with listener being handle, listening being true, complaint being ""
        when Result.Error holding why then
            give build bound-server with listener being 0, listening being false, complaint being why
        otherwise
            give build bound-server with listener being 0, listening being false,
                complaint being "the port could not be bound"
    end consider
end paragraph


public stop-server receives server as bound-server returns nothing begin paragraph
    when server.listening then
        evaluate nil.std.net::close with handle being server.listener
    end when
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- What one pass round the loop produced.
!!!
!!! `request` is the message as it arrived, for the application to answer.
!!! `served` false with an empty complaint is an ordinary non-event — a
!!! connection that closed before saying anything, which happens whenever a
!!! browser opens a speculative socket — and is not worth logging.

public accepted begin record
    field connection as number
    field accepted-ok as boolean
    field request as text
    field served as boolean
    field complaint as text
end record


!!! --- Accept one connection and read its request.
!!!
!!! Reads until the header section is complete and then until Content-Length
!!! is satisfied, rather than taking whatever one read returns: a request is a
!!! stream and arrives in as many pieces as the network feels like. A client
!!! that sends a header section and stops is ended by the deadline, not by
!!! this loop guessing.

public accept-request receives server as bound-server returns accepted begin paragraph
    when not server.listening then
        give build accepted with connection being 0, accepted-ok being false, request being "",
            served being false, complaint being "the server is not listening"
    end when

    value taken is nil.std.net::accept with handle being server.listener
    consider taken
        when Result.Error holding why then
            give build accepted with connection being 0, accepted-ok being false, request being "",
                served being false, complaint being why
        when Result.Ok holding connection then begin block
            evaluate nil.std.net::set_timeout with handle being connection, milliseconds being silence-limit-ms
            evaluate nil.std.net::set_no_delay with handle being connection, enabled being true
            give read-request with connection being connection
        end block
        otherwise
            give build accepted with connection being 0, accepted-ok being false, request being "",
                served being false, complaint being "accept gave no answer"
    end consider
end paragraph


read-request receives connection as number returns accepted begin paragraph
    variable gathered as text is ""
    variable finished as boolean is false
    variable complaint as text is ""

    repeat while not finished
        value heard is nil.std.net::read with handle being connection, maximum_bytes being chunk-size
        consider heard
            when Result.Error holding why then begin block
                set complaint to why
                set finished to true
            end block
            when Result.Ok holding piece then begin block
                !!! Flat rather than nested: a branch holding its own `when`
                !!! needs an explicit arm block, and four plain conditions are
                !!! easier to check than one with three tails.
                !!!
                !!! Empty means the peer closed its side. If nothing arrived
                !!! at all it was a connection that never asked anything.
                value closed is piece equals ""
                when closed then
                    set finished to true
                end when
                when not closed then
                    set gathered to gathered plus piece
                end when
                value too-large is (nil.std.text::length with s being gathered) is greater than request-limit
                when not closed and too-large then
                    set complaint to "the request is larger than this server accepts"
                    set finished to true
                end when
                when not closed and not too-large and (request-is-complete with message being gathered) then
                    set finished to true
                end when
            end block
            otherwise begin block
                set complaint to "the read gave no answer"
                set finished to true
            end block
        end consider
    end repeat

    value served is complaint equals "" and not (gathered equals "")
    give build accepted with connection being connection, accepted-ok being true,
        request being gathered, served being served, complaint being complaint
end paragraph


!!! --- Whether enough of the message has arrived to answer it.
!!!
!!! The header section ends at the first blank line. After that, a body is
!!! expected only if Content-Length says so — this server does not accept
!!! chunked transfer encoding, and a request that asks for it is answered by
!!! the layer above rather than waited on here.

public request-is-complete receives message as text returns boolean begin paragraph
    value marker is (crlf with nothing) plus (crlf with nothing)
    variable head-length as number is nil.std.text::index_of with s being message, needle being marker
    variable separator as number is 4
    when head-length is less than 0 then
        set head-length to nil.std.text::index_of with s being message, needle being newline plus newline
        set separator to 2
    end when
    when head-length is less than 0 then
        give false
    end when

    value head is nil.std.text::substring with s being message, start being 0, length being head-length
    value declared is declared-length with head being head
    when declared is at most 0 then
        give true
    end when
    value body-start is head-length plus separator
    value body-so-far is (nil.std.text::length with s being message) minus body-start
    give body-so-far is at least declared
end paragraph


!!! --- Content-Length from the header section, or zero when it is absent.
!!! A value that is not a number reads as zero, which means the body is not
!!! waited for; the parser above will reject the request on its own terms.

declared-length receives head as text returns number begin paragraph
    value lines is split-on with input being head, separator being newline
    repeat for each line in lines
        value trimmed is nil.std.text::trim with s being line
        value name is nil.std.text::trim with s being (before-first with input being trimmed, separator being ":")
        when same-folded with left being name, right being "Content-Length" then
            value stated is nil.std.text::trim with s being (after-first with input being trimmed, separator being ":")
            give digits-value with digits being stated
        end when
    end repeat
    give 0
end paragraph


!!! --- A decimal count, without borrowing a parser that raises on bad input.
!!! Anything that is not all digits is zero: a Content-Length a client made up
!!! must not be able to stop the server with a fault.

digits-value receives digits as text returns number begin paragraph
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being digits
    when width is less than 1 or width is greater than 18 then
        give 0
    end when
    variable total as number is 0
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than width
        value code is nil.std.text::byte_at with s being digits, index being index
        when code is less than 48 or code is greater than 57 then
            give 0
        end when
        set total to (total times 10) plus (code minus 48)
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give total
end paragraph


!!! --- Send a response and close.
!!!
!!! Always closes, including when the write failed: this server speaks no
!!! keep-alive, so the connection has no further use, and a connection left
!!! open after a failed write is a descriptor nobody will come back for.
!!! A failed write is reported rather than raised — a peer that left before
!!! its answer arrived is a Tuesday, not an error in the program.

public answer-and-close receives connection as number, response as text returns text begin paragraph
    variable complaint as text is ""
    value sent is nil.std.net::write with handle being connection, data being response
    consider sent
        when Result.Error holding why then set complaint to why
        otherwise set complaint to ""
    end consider
    evaluate nil.std.net::close with handle being connection
    give complaint
end paragraph


!!! --- Close a connection that is not going to be answered.

public discard receives connection as number returns nothing begin paragraph
    evaluate nil.std.net::close with handle being connection
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- Where the server can be reached, for the line printed at startup.

public address-text receives host as text, port as number returns text begin paragraph
    value shown is when host equals "" give "0.0.0.0" otherwise give host end when
    give "http://" plus shown plus ":" plus (port becomes text) plus "/"
end paragraph
